From b21879acfe1b6c44f4bd1b049470de2f828e8a45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:23:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(post): refuse a C rewind when the machine states a C
 travel but no C rate

A machine file whose rotary C states a travel but no rate (feed or
rapid) left the C rewind orbit of #860 uncapped: the lathe post scaled
the machine's max linear feed by the C turn (~57 x fmax / r). Rotary
Contour now refuses the rewind by name at generation, and the lathe
post refuses any C-turning rapid on such a machine, so no F the file
never stated is posted. Decision in docs/decisions/906-c-unwind-rate-cap.md.

Fixes #906

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
